{"kind":"assert","text":"S4 Native follow-up: run the whole Native step once, not the 104-file complement\n\nThis answers 7cdf2cd9 and the proposed question in /private/tmp/artroom-s4-native-remainder-analysis-20261031-v1. My answer to that question is no. If I receive the composed evidence at review, I will not accept it as the follow-up. The planner can overrule this answer.\n\nThe rule in `docs/testing.md`, \"Follow-up after a gate\", asks for \"the steps the gate never reached\". Gate two never reached Native, so the follow-up owes one Native step. The 149 module records have no run end, no final rows and no unhandled-error count, as your plan says. A new subset can't supply those for the old files, so the composed evidence would leave the step unfinished for good.\n\nThe missing proof is a terminal record for all 253 files in one run. This witness supplies it:\n\n1. Run compatibility preparation and the unchanged Native stage once at a8c409df, tree cea78b8e, with the same configs, project order, worker limits, assertions and deadlines.\n2. Raise each stream's capture limit to the 128 MiB you propose, and keep the 2,400-second budget. Do not mute output.\n3. Keep the interrupted attempt as inconclusive, and report it beside the new run. An overflow at 128 MiB stays inconclusive and comes back to the planner.\n\nDo not rerun the compilers, the wire owner, Node, Counting or Plain. Your earlier results for those steps stand for this assessment.\n\nThis run does not break the rule against repeating whole suites, because Native has never finished at this source. It also costs little: the interrupted attempt covered 149 of the 253 files in 680 seconds, and the subset would still need its own start, its filter review and a composed report.\n\nThe stop came from the follow-up's own 32 MiB limit, and nothing in it points at the source. The diff from ce168eef to a8c409df is one line in `packages/mcp/test/wire.test.ts`, and it changes only the fake. I will assess the repair and the evidence together at review. Both ordinary gates stay failed.\n\nThis note releases no room, provider or live action.","body":{"to":"builder"}}